From: GLM-EXL3-2x-GB10 testing line <tensorfold-zig-testing@local>
Subject: glm-cuda: the E4M3 Tables' page_rows = 512, not the whole-page-stride formula (the contamination root cause)

PROVENANCE: this line's fix, 2026-11-05, on the marriage port. The Table
sites computed page_rows = c.ps/(l.lw*2) - the WHOLE-page stride over the
bf16 row bytes - 3,481 for E4M3 instead of 512. The selection kernel
indexes pt[row/page_rows]: with 3,481 every row below 3,481 reads page 0's
pooled keys, the token selection scores against rows 0-511's keys, and the
sparse lists are garbage (the hardmode battery's cross-request-content
signature; the canary receipts). The contract tests passed because their
fixtures use per-layer ps, where the formula coincidentally yields 512; the
engine's Caches carry the whole-page ps. bf16 keeps its formula (its lists
are page rows, a different unit; its path is receipted correct).
OWNER: this line; STATUS: the contamination fix, judged by the canary +
the battery re-run.

diff --git a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_dsa_block.zig b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_dsa_block.zig
index efc2675..f143179 100644
--- a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_dsa_block.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_dsa_block.zig
@@ -137,7 +137,7 @@ pub fn attend(k: Kernels, stream: cuda.Stream, l: Layer, c: Caches, s: Scratch,
     v.qi += r0 * ix.heads * ix.d * 2;
     try writeKeys(k, stream, l, c, v, rows, pos);
     // an E4M3 cache's sparse lists stay positions (its chunks take each key through the table); BF16's are page rows
-    const t: latent.Table = .{ .pt = c.pt, .ps = c.ps, .page_rows = c.ps / (l.lw * 2), .logical = c.ls != 0 };
+    const t: latent.Table = .{ .pt = c.pt, .ps = c.ps, .page_rows = if (c.ls != 0) latent.chunk else c.ps / (l.lw * 2), .logical = c.ls != 0 };
     const tk: latent.Table = .{ .pt = c.pt, .ps = if (c.pks != 0) c.pks else c.ps, .page_rows = t.page_rows };
     const scale: f32 = @floatCast(std.math.pow(f64, @floatFromInt(l.qk), -0.5));
     if (host_pos < l.dense_limit) {
@@ -165,7 +165,7 @@ pub fn attend(k: Kernels, stream: cuda.Stream, l: Layer, c: Caches, s: Scratch,
